 "amendments": {
  "P1_collapse_is_a_theoretical_identity": "The SLLOD + linear-spring + Coulomb system is exactly invariant under (k_n, gamma_dot) -> (lambda^2 k_n, lambda gamma_dot) with time rescaled by 1/lambda: the equations map onto themselves and kappa is unchanged. Because the time step is defined as a fixed fraction of t_c = sqrt(m/k_n), the discrete trajectory is the same as well, so tau* is bit-for-bit identical. P1 therefore verifies that the kernel carries NO hidden absolute time, length or unit scale (an implementation invariant, and it would fail if dt were fixed in absolute time or the neighbour skin were in physical units) -- it is NOT empirical evidence for Campbell's similarity hypothesis, which no constant-stiffness experiment could supply in the first place.",
  "physics_legs_are_P2_P3_P4_only": "The empirical content of this round is the SHAPE of f(kappa): the exponent and its drift, not the collapse.",
  "global_beta_is_an_average_over_a_curved_curve": "The local exponent runs from ~0.89 to ~0.98 across the grid, so the global beta is an average; the elastic-limit estimate is beta_high_half.",
  "energy_audit_is_the_limiting_gate": "The energy-audit defect reaches the gate value (0.30) at the stiffest contacts; points passing at a defect near the gate are less trustworthy than their neighbours, which is why the top-decade exponent carries the larger uncertainty.",
  "rejected_point_is_physics_not_bug": "kn1e5_g0.5 (kappa=2.3e5) failed only the steady-state drift gate; it is reported as rejected and excluded from every fit rather than re-run until it passed."
 },
